{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "patient-care",
    "title": "Patient Care",
    "order": 4
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "communication-patient-education",
    "title": "Communication & Patient Education",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "Communication Is the Job, Not a Soft Skill",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Securing a patient's cooperation, day after day, through simulation and every treatment fraction, is one of the most important and most challenging parts of being a radiation therapist. Communication and patient safety go hand in hand \u2014 a patient who understands and trusts you is a patient who holds still, follows instructions, and tells you when something feels wrong."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "All communication with patients must be "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "patient-focused, accurate, timely, and within your scope of practice",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Human Diversity and Cultural Competency",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Every patient brings their own age, race, religion, ethnicity, gender identity, ability, and life circumstances into the treatment room. None of that is a barrier to good care \u2014 it's context you need to work with."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Four core values underpin respectful, rights-based care: "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "autonomy, dignity, equality, and solidarity",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": ". Consent for treatment cannot happen without sensitivity to a patient's cultural and language needs \u2014 use professional interpreters, not family members, whenever language is a barrier."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Becoming culturally competent is a process: recognize diversity as a value, build awareness of how cross-cultural interactions play out, and practice honest self-assessment of your own assumptions."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Verbal and Nonverbal Communication",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Verbal communication",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " includes spoken and written words \u2014 and also slang, jargon, and humor, all of which can land very differently than intended with an anxious patient."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Nonverbal communication",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (sometimes called paralanguage) often says more than your words: body language, touch, professional appearance, physical presence, eye contact, and personal hygiene all shape whether a patient feels safe with you."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page3_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Which of the following is an example of nonverbal communication?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Explaining the treatment schedule out loud",
              "Maintaining eye contact and an open posture",
              "Reading the physician's written order"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Eye contact and posture are nonverbal (paralanguage) cues, unlike spoken explanations or written orders."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Age, Impairments, and Communication Challenges",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Age is "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "not",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " a barrier to effective communication \u2014 but it does change your approach. With older patients: maintain eye contact, speak clearly and a bit more slowly, speak "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "to",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " them rather than around them, and treat them with patience and respect."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Language barriers, cultural and social factors, and physical, sensory, or cognitive impairments all call for the same underlying skill: slow down, check understanding frequently, and adjust your explanation rather than repeating the same words louder."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Terminal Patients",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Radiation oncology staff work with terminal patients often. Death is part of the natural cycle of life, and healthcare's attitude toward it has shifted toward being more open and more respectful of a dying patient's own wishes."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Patients, families, and loved ones need to move through grief in their own individualized timeframe. "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Patient autonomy",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " \u2014 respecting the choices a patient makes about their own care and how they want to spend their remaining time \u2014 is central here."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Communicating with Family and Friends",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Before you say anything to a patient's family or friends about their condition or care, you need the patient's permission \u2014 otherwise you risk a "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "HIPAA violation",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", regardless of good intentions."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "When you do have permission: introduce yourself professionally, briefly explain the procedure, and explain why they need to step out of the room during beam-on. Empathy toward family members is just as powerful as empathy toward the patient."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page6_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A patient's adult child asks you how the treatment is going. What should you do first?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Give a brief, reassuring summary since they're clearly family",
              "Confirm the patient has given permission to share information with this person"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Being family doesn't automatically grant access to health information \u2014 you need the patient's permission first, every time."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The AIDET Framework",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "AIDET",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is a widely used structure for consistent, compassionate patient communication:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "A",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "cknowledge \u2014 greet the patient by name, make eye contact"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "I",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "ntroduce \u2014 yourself, your role, and your experience"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "D",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "uration \u2014 how long the visit or step will take"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "E",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "xplanation \u2014 what you're about to do and why"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "T",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "hank you \u2014 for their time, patience, or trust"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Running through AIDET at each new step of a visit turns a routine interaction into one that feels respectful and predictable \u2014 which matters enormously to an anxious patient."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Patient Education",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Part of your role is explaining, in plain language: the purpose of a treatment or procedure, how long it will take, and what dose or exposure is involved. You'll also field questions comparing radiation therapy to other imaging modalities, and reinforce pre- and post-treatment instructions (skin care, diet, medications)."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Clear education supports "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "treatment compliance",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " \u2014 a patient who understands why they need to hold still, keep their positioning marks, or follow a skin-care routine is far more likely to actually do it."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Support Services",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You're one part of a larger care team. Know when and how to loop in:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Hospice",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 for patients transitioning to comfort-focused, palliative care"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Dietitians",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 for nutrition and side-effect management"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Clergy / chaplaincy",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 for spiritual support"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Social workers",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 for financial, transportation, or family support needs"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Recognizing when a patient needs support beyond what you can offer \u2014 and knowing who to call \u2014 is itself a communication skill."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've covered cultural competency, verbal and nonverbal communication, age and impairment-related adjustments, terminal patient care, family communication and HIPAA, the AIDET framework, patient education, and the broader support team."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "None of this replaces clinical judgment in the moment \u2014 but it gives you a consistent foundation to build on with every patient you meet."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
